  "notes": "Earlier label and pressing variation. Green label pressing with 'WB' logo, pressed by [l403953] as indicated by 'T 1' in runouts.\n\nLabels state \"Produced by Bob Matthews and Betty Cantor in association with the Grateful Dead\" but does not have Executive Producer credit. Includes [l267310] logo stamped in runout. \n\nDiffers from [r=5180677] which has \"Executive Producer: Bob Matthews\" text on labels and 'KD' in runout etchings.\n\nRough textured cardboard cover, with rear slick pasted on upside down.\n\nAll selections Ice Nine Publishing Company (ASCAP)\n\nRecorded at Pacific High Recording Studio, San Francisco. Engineered by Alembic.\n\nFrom rear cover:\nWarner Bros. Records Inc., a Subsidiary & Licensee of Warner Bros. Inc., 4000 Warner Blvd., Burbank, Calif. · 488 Madison Ave., New York, N.Y. Made in U.S.A. © 1970 - Warner Bros. Records Inc.",
  "released_formatted": "14 Jun 1970",
